  "id": "COMPOUND:43986 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 13-O-acetylphorbol-20-oleate and DNA polymerase iota, as this compound is identified as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately interact with DNA polymerase iota. Specifically, 13-O-acetylphorbol-20-oleate is a target of Decursitin B and Kadlongilactone A, both of which are known to interact with DNA polymerase iota. Similarly, 13-O-acetylphorbol-20-oleate is also a target of HL-60, which is targeted by Mulberrofuran F, another compound that interacts with DNA polymerase iota. These findings collectively indicate that 13-O-acetylphorbol-20-oleate may serve as a mediator in the pathway leading to DNA polymerase iota, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The scores from the different paths suggest a consistent pattern of interaction, but the strength of the evidence varies, reflecting the complexity of the biological network involved.",
